From 6a6140535ca7eaa267384b555e9039ffb5bc4394 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TDVP Build <tdvp@local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 19:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] protocol: use the Buildroot host wayland-scanner

gtk-layer-shell first consults the target wayland-scanner pkg-config
variable.  In a cross build that variable is /usr/bin/wayland-scanner,
which refers to a program in the target rootfs rather than a tool that is
available while building.  Buildroot provides the matching scanner through
host-wayland and places HOST_DIR/bin on PATH.

Always resolve the generator from PATH, so Meson selects the Buildroot host
tool and never embeds or executes a target-rootfs path during configuration.

Signed-off-by: TDVP Build <tdvp@local>
---
 protocol/meson.build | 6 +-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/protocol/meson.build b/protocol/meson.build
index 7fe5dfc..e2e32e3 100644
--- a/protocol/meson.build
+++ b/protocol/meson.build
@@ -1,8 +1,4 @@
-if wayland_scanner.found()
-    prog_wayland_scanner = find_program(wayland_scanner.get_pkgconfig_variable('wayland_scanner'))
-else
-    prog_wayland_scanner = find_program('wayland-scanner')
-endif
+prog_wayland_scanner = find_program('wayland-scanner')

 protocols = [
     'wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1.xml'
--
